  "why": "The statement names no field, but abundance is conventionally a characteristic-zero conjecture and the claim in openai-math-034 (projective lc pairs, all dimensions, any algebraically closed char-0 field) contains the bullet's klt, Delta=0 case as worded; I read it as whole, unreviewed and doubtful rather than case, since restricting to algebraically closed char 0 is the standard setting rather than a narrowing. 036's main manuscript assumes log abundance as an input, so it is a conditional reduction (none). 035 (threefolds, nu=1, p>3) and 051 (smooth Brody-hyperbolic Kahler, hence projective, with K ample) are restricted classes of the bullet: case. Human in-window work: Iwai-Matsumura-Muller is a case digested by Proc. LMS acceptance; Liu-Xu's unconditional smooth dim<=5 nu<=1 results are a case; Lazic and Fujino 2025 are conditional reductions; Kahler, slc, nonvanishing, deformation and log-surface results are variants (the klt surface case was already known). The AI role for each OpenAI event rests on the README's statement that results were obtained with an internal model, which I read as generated.",
